sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C as Citizen / Operator
    participant UI as SevaOne UI (React)
    participant BFF as SevaOne BFF (.NET 10)
    participant R as Redis Cache
    participant PG as PostgreSQL
    participant IS as WSO2 Identity Server (9443)
    participant GW as WSO2 APIM (Gateway 8243)
    participant D as Department System<br/>(URL 1 and URL 2 caller)
    participant S as Department or Sakala GSE<br/>(URL 3 Status API)

    Note over C,PG: Phase 1: Login (already in place). Citizen or operator signs in through WSO2 Identity Server
    C->>UI: Log in (citizen: OTP or DigiLocker, operator: franchise login)
    UI->>BFF: POST /api/v1/auth/... or /api/v1/operator/login
    BFF->>IS: SCIM2 find-or-create, then JWT-bearer grant (citizen, operator or admin issuer)
    IS-->>BFF: Access and refresh tokens
    BFF-->>UI: HttpOnly session cookies

    Note over C,PG: Phase 2: Handoff. WSO2 Identity Server mints the Token
    C->>UI: Click Apply on a department service
    UI->>BFF: POST /api/v1/departments/{dept}/schemes/{code}/apply-token
    BFF->>PG: Create the handoff (unique edcsApplicationRefNo, user, assistedmode, ServiceId)
    BFF->>IS: JWT-bearer grant: signed assertion with scope dept:{code} svc:{id}
    IS-->>BFF: Opaque access token (the Token, single use, 30 min)
    BFF->>PG: Store the Token hash against the handoff
    BFF-->>UI: Form fields: UserId, edcsApplicationRefNo, Token, assistedmode, ServiceId
    UI-->>C: Auto-submitting POST form to the department

    Note over C,D: Phase 3: URL 1. The department works exactly as it does with Seva Sindhu today
    C->>D: POST form to the Department URL (URL 1)
    opt Department asks SevaOne to check the Token (method not defined yet)
        D->>GW: Token check API (Basic credentials)
        GW->>IS: Introspect the Token (client credentials held at the gateway)
        IS-->>GW: {active, scope}
        GW-->>D: Valid or invalid
    end
    D-->>C: HTTP 200, access allowed
    C->>D: Fill the application form and pay the department fee

    Note over D,PG: Phase 4: URL 2. The acknowledgement comes in through WSO2 APIM
    D->>D: Generate the final acknowledgement
    D->>GW: POST /api/TokenIntegration/department-update (JSON, Authorization: Basic)
    Note right of GW: APIM checks the Basic credentials, the IP allow-list,<br/>the department's throttle tier and the payload size.<br/>It adds the department identity and the gateway secret.
    GW->>BFF: Forward with department identity and gateway secret
    BFF->>R: Look up the Token verdict
    alt Cache miss
        BFF->>IS: POST /oauth2/introspect
        IS-->>BFF: {active: true, scope: "dept:{code}"}
        BFF->>R: Cache the verdict (60 s at most)
    end
    Note right of BFF: The scope department must equal the Basic credentials' department.<br/>The Token must match the stored handoff and EdcsApplicationRefNo.
    alt Token valid and handoff matches
        BFF->>PG: Save payment details and acknowledgement (idempotent on the two reference numbers)
        BFF->>PG: Set status to SUCCESS, write the outbox event
        BFF->>IS: Revoke the Token (single use is now complete)
        BFF-->>GW: {DepartmentApplicationUpdateId, EdcsApplicationRefNo, DepartmentApplicationRefNo}
        GW-->>D: 200 with the same body
        D-->>C: Redirect the browser back to SevaOne
        C->>UI: Return to SevaOne
        UI->>BFF: Get the acknowledgement
        BFF->>PG: Read the saved response
        BFF-->>UI: Acknowledgement to print
    else Token invalid or save failed
        BFF-->>GW: {"Message": "Data Not Inserted"}
        GW-->>D: Failure body
        BFF->>PG: Show the transaction as Failed
        Note over D,GW: The department calls URL 2 again until it succeeds
    end

    Note over BFF,S: Phase 5: URL 3. SevaOne checks the status through an outbound WSO2 APIM API
    loop Whenever SevaOne needs the status
        BFF->>GW: GET status for the department (outbound API)
        GW->>S: POST {GscNumber} (retry, timeout and throttle at the gateway)
        S-->>GW: Application status
        GW-->>BFF: Application status
        BFF->>PG: Update the status timeline
    end
